What kind of tortoise is this?

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.630
Anyway, this is what they used.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.790
Once the material latex was invented,

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.910
condoms became very cheap
and widely available,

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.070
but you have to understand
that, for a long time,

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.780
they weren't trying to not have kids.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.360
They were trying to stop
diseases from spreading.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.430
- [Announcer] But you don't
get them if you use a condom.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.860
- Because children are
a blessing from above.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.360
Why would you want to not have them?

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.104
- [Woman] Let me see what you have.

00:12:14.104 --> 00:12:15.087
- A knife!
- No!

00:12:15.087 --> 00:12:17.280
- But then women in the modern age,

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:20.610
heaven forbid, wanted
to have fewer children,

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:22.830
but they still wanted to
have sex, and unfortunately,

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.350
a top way of doing that
was through dangerous

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.330
and deadly back-alley abortions.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:31.200
So in 1916, this nurse from
New York opened a clinic,

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.660
and the theme of her
clinic was birth control,

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:36.300
teaching women how not to get pregnant.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:38.610
By the way, this was like
super illegal at the time

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.020
because under this law,

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.020
you couldn't publish anything
having to do with sex.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:46.050
So she's totally breaking the
law teaching women about sex.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:47.610
Geez, scandalous.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:48.540
But she fought back

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.330
and eventually helped
create Planned Parenthood.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:55.830
And it was her who led the
charge in creating the pill,

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.890
the thing that uses hormones
to stop reproduction

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:01.050
from happening, and in the 60s,

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.600
this pill would change everything.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:06.210
- Equal rights to have
a job, to have respect

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.760
and not be viewed as a piece of meat.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.170
- Women have a fundamental right

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:13.350
to control their own bodies,
to control their own lives.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.930
- Women could now have
autonomy over their bodies.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.570
They could go to work and
earn money for themselves

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:21.630
and decide for themselves when
they wanted to have children.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:26.070
She was a hero, a liberator,
and she was totally racist,

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.950
or at least she spoke about
it in a very racist parlance,

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.727
referring to it as a tool to help, quote,

00:13:30.727 --> 00:13:32.880
"the process of weeding out the unfit

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.730
and preventing the birth of defectives."

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:36.690
That's more than racist.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.160
That's called eugenics,

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.010
which was a popular pseudoscientific
movement at the time

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.410
that was all about
breeding a superior race

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.000
and eradicating the unfit,

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.130
which these people were able
to deem whoever they wanted.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.960
Poor people, people of color, immigrants,

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.960
people with disabilities, all
of them were to be weeded out.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:54.480
So a inconvenient fact in all of the story

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.730
is that a major motivation for the pill

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.010
wasn't sexual liberation, but rather,

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.110
it was the overpopulation of the earth

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.720
with these unfit races and peoples.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.480
But nonetheless, the development
of the pill went forward,

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.100
and they decided to do trials on it

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.450
to get it ready for market,

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.220
and where did they turn but Puerto Rico,

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.030
a place where all problems
were blamed on overpopulation,

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:18.510
a perfect testing grounds
for this really twisted,

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:22.140
F'ed up project of
weeding out unfit races.

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:22.980
- [Announcer] Puerto Rico,

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.170
a beautiful little island
with a big problem.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:28.560
- [Woman] In 1956,
contraceptive pills 20 times

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:31.350
as strong as the ones used
today were first tested

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.060
among Puerto Rican women who lived

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.770
in government housing projects.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.200
- In Puerto Rico, they were
already sterilizing women

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.730
to control the population,

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.490
and now they were gonna test
out this new experimental pill.

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:43.710
They pitched them like,
"Hey, come do the pill

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.420
instead of getting sterilized,"

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.860
because they were literally forcing people

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.230
to get surgery where they tie the tubes

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.180
and they like make it
impossible to have kids.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.800
They started giving them the pill.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.060
Oh, but they forgot to tell them

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:55.410
that they're a part of a trial

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.120
for a highly experimental drug

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.816
that was gonna mess with their hormones.

00:14:58.816 --> 00:15:03.816
(speaks in foreign language)
(soft dramatic music)

00:15:06.598 --> 00:15:10.431
(speaks in foreign language)

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:25.560
- These doctors didn't have
their dosing figured out yet.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.390
So they were giving women pills

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:30.600
that were way more hormonally aggressive

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.010
than the ones we have today.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:34.890
So these women were experiencing
intense side effects,

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:37.470
but the doctors running the
trial told the "New York Times"

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:41.220
that these side effects were,
quote, "largely psychogenic,"

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:44.100
most of them happening
because women expect them.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.960
22 women dropped out of the study

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:49.650
because of the side effects,
and three women died,

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:51.360
but their deaths were never investigated.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:53.700
But in the end, the trial
was deemed a success.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.310
Eventually, they dialed in the dosage,

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.960
and the pill hit the market,

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:59.760
and that's how we got
the birth control pill.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.200
I wish it was a better story.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:02.033
Like I wish there

00:16:02.033 --> 00:16:03.960
